{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"The post 'Sunsetting Create React App' was published February 14, 2025 by Matt Carroll and Ricky Hanlon.","source_span":"February 14, 2025 by [Matt Carroll]...and [Ricky Hanlon]"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"The React team is deprecating Create React App for new apps.","source_span":"Today, we’re deprecating [Create React App] for new apps"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"Existing apps are encouraged to migrate to a framework or to a build tool like Vite, Parcel, or RSBuild.","source_span":"encouraging existing apps to migrate to a framework...or to migrate to a build tool...like Vite, Parcel, or RSBuild"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"Create React App was released in 2016.","source_span":"When we released Create React App in 2016"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"Create React App currently has no active maintainers, which is a key reason for its deprecation.","source_span":"since Create React App currently has no active maintainers"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"Starting February 14, 2025, installing a new app with Create React App shows a deprecation warning that appears only once per install.","source_span":"Starting today, if you install a new app, you will see a deprecation warning...This error message will only be shown once per install."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"Create React App will continue working in maintenance mode, and a new version was published to work with React 19.","source_span":"Create React App will continue working in maintenance mode, and we've published a new version of Create React App to work with React 19."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"All the frameworks React recommends support client-side rendering (CSR) and single-page apps (SPA), and can be deployed to a CDN or static hosting service without a server.","source_span":"All the frameworks we recommend support client-side rendering ([CSR])...and single-page apps ([SPA])...and can be deployed to a CDN or static hosting service without a server."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"For existing apps migrating to a client-only SPA, migration guides are provided for Next.js, React Router, and Expo Router.","source_span":"Next.js’ Create React App migration guide...React Router’s framework adoption guide...Expo webpack to Expo Router migration guide"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"For existing apps migrating to a build tool, migration guides are provided for Vite, Parcel, and Rsbuild.","source_span":"Vite Create React App migration guide...Parcel Create React App migration guide...Rsbuild Create React App migration guide"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","statement":"Running `npx create-react-app my-app` produces a fully configured React app with a development server, linting, and a production build.","source_span":"After running `npx create-react-app my-app`, you get a fully configured React app with a development server, linting, and a production build."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","fact_refs":[0],"question":"When was the 'Sunsetting Create React App' announcement published and who wrote it?","answer":"It was published on February 14, 2025, and written by Matt Carroll and Ricky Hanlon."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","fact_refs":[3],"question":"In what year was Create React App originally released?","answer":"Create React App was released in 2016."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","fact_refs":[4],"question":"Why did the React team decide to deprecate Create React App rather than evolve it into a framework?","answer":"Because Create React App currently has no active maintainers, and many existing frameworks already solve the problems it would need to evolve to address."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","fact_refs":[5,6,7],"question":"What happens now when you install a new app with Create React App, and will it stop working entirely?","answer":"You see a deprecation warning (shown once per install) pointing to react.dev for up-to-date frameworks. Create React App itself will keep working in maintenance mode, and a new version was published to support React 19."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","fact_refs":[9,10],"question":"What migration guides does React provide for moving away from Create React App?","answer":"For moving to a framework: Next.js, React Router, and Expo Router migration guides. For moving to a build tool: Vite, Parcel, and Rsbuild migration guides."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_sunsetting-create-react-app","fact_refs":[8],"question":"What rendering capabilities do the frameworks recommended by React support?","answer":"All recommended frameworks support client-side rendering (CSR) and single-page apps (SPA), and can be deployed to a CDN or static hosting service without needing a server."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"'React Labs: View Transitions, Activity, and more' was published April 23, 2025 by Ricky Hanlon.","source_span":"April 23, 2025 by [Ricky Hanlon]"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"Two new experimental features announced as ready to try are View Transitions and Activity.","source_span":"we're sharing two new experimental features that are ready to try today"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"The <Activity /> component has shipped in react@19.2.","source_span":"`<Activity />` has shipped in `react@19.2`."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"<ViewTransition /> and addTransitionType are available in react@canary.","source_span":"`<ViewTransition />` and `addTransitionType` are now available in `react@canary`."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"To try View Transitions and Activity, you upgrade React packages to react@experimental and react-dom@experimental.","source_span":"You can try them by upgrading React packages to the most recent experimental version:\n\n- `react@experimental`\n- `react-dom@experimental`"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"React View Transitions use the browser's startViewTransition API under the hood.","source_span":"these animations use the new [`startViewTransition`]...API available in most modern browsers"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"There are three triggers for a View Transition: Transitions (startTransition), Deferred Values (useDeferredValue), and Suspense.","source_span":"You can define \"when\" to animate by using one of these three triggers for a View Transition"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","statement":"The post also shares updates on features in development: React Performance Tracks, Compiler IDE Extension, Automatic Effect Dependencies, Fragment Refs, and Concurrent Stores.","source_span":"We're also sharing updates on new features currently in development:\n- [React Performance Tracks]...\n- [Compiler IDE Extension]...\n- [Automatic Effect Dependencies]...\n- [Fragment Refs]...\n- [Concurrent Stores]"}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","fact_refs":[0],"question":"Who wrote the April 2025 React Labs post about View Transitions and Activity, and when was it published?","answer":"It was written by Ricky Hanlon and published on April 23, 2025."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","fact_refs":[1],"question":"Which two new experimental React features were announced as ready to try in this React Labs post?","answer":"View Transitions and Activity."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","fact_refs":[2,3],"question":"Which React release channel did the Activity component ship in, and where are ViewTransition and addTransitionType available?","answer":"Activity shipped in react@19.2, while ViewTransition and addTransitionType are available in react@canary."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","fact_refs":[4],"question":"How do you try React's experimental View Transitions and Activity features?","answer":"By upgrading React packages to the most recent experimental versions: react@experimental and react-dom@experimental."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What browser API do React View Transitions rely on under the hood?","answer":"They use the browser's startViewTransition API, available in most modern browsers."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What are the three triggers that can activate a React View Transition?","answer":"Transitions (via startTransition), Deferred Values (via useDeferredValue), and Suspense."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-labs-view-transitions-activity-and-more","fact_refs":[7],"question":"Besides View Transitions and Activity, what other in-development features did this React Labs update mention?","answer":"React Performance Tracks, Compiler IDE Extension, Automatic Effect Dependencies, Fragment Refs, and Concurrent Stores."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"React 19.2 was released on npm on October 1, 2025, announced by The React Team.","source_span":"October 1, 2025 by [The React Team]...React 19.2 is now available on npm!"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"React 19.2 is the third release in the last year, following React 19 in December and React 19.1 in June.","source_span":"This is our third release in the last year, following React 19 in December and React 19.1 in June."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"In React 19.2, Activity supports two modes: visible and hidden.","source_span":"In React 19.2, Activity supports two modes: `visible` and `hidden`."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"The hidden Activity mode hides the children, unmounts effects, and defers all updates until React has nothing left to work on.","source_span":"`hidden`: hides the children, unmounts effects, and defers all updates until React has nothing left to work on."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"The visible Activity mode shows the children, mounts effects, and allows updates to be processed normally.","source_span":"`visible`: shows the children, mounts effects, and allows updates to be processed normally."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"useEffectEvent lets you split the 'event' part of Effect logic out of the Effect that emits it, so it isn't treated as a dependency.","source_span":"With `useEffectEvent`, you can split the \"event\" part of this logic out of the Effect that emits it"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"To use useEffectEvent correctly with linting support, you need to upgrade to eslint-plugin-react-hooks@latest.","source_span":"You'll need to upgrade to `eslint-plugin-react-hooks@latest` so that the linter doesn't try to insert them as dependencies."}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"cacheSignal is only for use with React Server Components.","source_span":"`cacheSignal` is only for use with [React Server Components]"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"cacheSignal lets you know when the cache() lifetime is over, such as when rendering completes successfully, is aborted, or fails.","source_span":"This allows you to clean up or abort work when the result will no longer be used in the cache, such as:\n\n- React has successfully completed rendering\n- The render was aborted\n- The render has failed"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"React 19.2 adds a new set of custom tracks to Chrome DevTools performance profiles, called Performance Tracks.","source_span":"React 19.2 adds a new set of [custom tracks]...to Chrome DevTools performance profiles to provide more information about the performance of your React app"}
{"type":"fact","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","statement":"The Scheduler track shows what React is working on for different priorities, such as 'blocking' for user interactions or 'transition' for updates inside startTransition.","source_span":"The Scheduler track shows what React is working on for different priorities such as \"blocking\" for user interactions, or \"transition\" for updates inside startTransition."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","fact_refs":[0,1],"question":"When was React 19.2 released, and which release in the past year is it?","answer":"React 19.2 was released on npm on October 1, 2025, and it is the third release in the last year, following React 19 in December and React 19.1 in June."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","fact_refs":[2,3,4],"question":"What are the two modes of the Activity component in React 19.2 and what does each do?","answer":"Activity supports 'visible' mode, which shows children, mounts effects, and processes updates normally, and 'hidden' mode, which hides children, unmounts effects, and defers all updates until React has nothing left to work on."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","fact_refs":[5],"question":"What problem does useEffectEvent solve in React 19.2?","answer":"It lets you split the 'event' part of an Effect's logic out of the Effect itself, so that value changes (like a theme prop) used only in that event logic don't cause the Effect to re-run."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","fact_refs":[6],"question":"What do you need to upgrade to get correct linter support for useEffectEvent?","answer":"You need to upgrade to eslint-plugin-react-hooks@latest."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","fact_refs":[7,8],"question":"What is cacheSignal used for and when does it indicate the cache lifetime has ended?","answer":"cacheSignal is only for use with React Server Components; it lets you know the cache() lifetime is over when rendering has completed successfully, was aborted, or has failed."}
{"type":"seed","doc_id":"d3_react_react-19-2","fact_refs":[9,10],"question":"What does the Scheduler track in React 19.2's Performance Tracks show?","answer":"It's a custom Chrome DevTools performance track showing what React is working on at different priorities, such as 'blocking' for user interactions or 'transition' for updates inside startTransition."}
